<a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/broadcasts/id1469995354">Broadcasts</a> app developer <a href="https://mastodon.social/@stroughtonsmith">Steve Troughton-Smith</a> has shared a Halloween treat for us today: a tour of the software on Apple's upcoming <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/apple-announces-homeview-smart-home-hub/">HomeView</a> smart home hub. Apple has already demoed the HomeView to selected tech reporters and content creators, but Troughton-Smith offers a closer look at several features, interfaces, and apps.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/homeview-entertainment-feature-1.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1071439" /><br/>
Using a virtualized HomeView created by <a href="https://mastodon.social/@_inside">Guilherme Rambo</a>, Troughton-Smith provided a closer look at the home screen, Control Center, clock faces like Flow and Snoopy, and apps like Timers, Alarms, World Clock, and Settings. Note that while the virtualized HomeView shows an Ethernet menu, the device actually supports Wi-Fi only.<br/>
<br/>
<div style="text-align: center;"><iframe src="https://mastodon.social/@stroughtonsmith/117535714058540414/embed" style="width: 100%; max-width: 540px; height: 725px; border: 0;" loading="lazy"></iframe><br/>
</div><br/>
<div style="clear: both;"></div><br/>
<br/>
HomeView supports up to six users. The device has a built-in camera that can recognize people and display their personal content in apps like Messages, Calendar, Reminders, FaceTime, and Find My. Rambo and Troughton-Smith have yet to bypass this recognition requirement  with the virtualized HomeView, so those apps are all locked.<br/>
<br/>
Troughton-Smith revealed that the HomeView will have a Liquid Glass slider that lets you adjust how clear or tinted the interface elements look, and he also confirmed that the device's keyboard supports QuickPath swipe typing.<br/>
<br/>
<div style="text-align: center;"><iframe src="https://mastodon.social/@stroughtonsmith/117533016105426071/embed" style="width: 100%; max-width: 540px; height: 800px; border: 0;" loading="lazy"></iframe><br/>
</div><br/>
<div style="clear: both;"></div><br/>
<br/>
He also provided a closer look at the HomeView's <a href="https://mastodon.social/@stroughtonsmith/117533061417431287">music player</a>, <a href="https://mastodon.social/@stroughtonsmith/117533078526193876">video player</a> in both wide and square formats, and <a href="https://mastodon.social/@stroughtonsmith/117533061417431287">AirPlay pairing interface</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Yesterday, Rambo and our contributor Aaron Perris provided a look at the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/30/homeview-software-27-2/">HomeView's wallpapers, "hello" setup screen, and more</a>. All of these findings come after Apple released the HomeView's software ahead of the device's launch on Friday, November 13. Apple is currently accepting pre-orders, with U.S. pricing set at &#36;299.<br/>
